Variable Assignemnt:

SECTION A: INPUT PARAMETERS


From Transaction/CDT:
- USER_CODE
- AUTO_TRANSACTION_NUMBER
- TRANSACTION_TYPE
- TRANSACTION_MODE
- SCHEME_CODE
- NAV_SERIAL_NO
- TRADE_DATE
- SUB_TRANSACTION_TYPE
- FOLIO_NUMBER
- PACKAGE_NAME
- INSURANCE_ID
- SIP_FLAG
- PAYMENT_MECHANISM
- PAYOUT_MECHANISM
- PERIODICITY
- GUARDIAN_DATE_OF_BIRTH
- SIP_REGISTRATION_DATE
- REMARKS
- APPLICATION_NUMBER
- USER_TRANSACTION_NUMBER
- TRANSACTION_NATURE
- PARENT_SUB_FUND_CODE
- LINK_SCHEME_CODE (input parameter, can be NULL)
- Entry_Date
- Amount
- Units
- Post_Validate_Flag (default 'V')
- IPO_CDT_Flag (source indicator: 'C'=CDT, 'I'=IPO, 'S'=SIP)
- New_Purch_Typ_Flag (optional input)
- Decimal_Amount
- SC_Closing_Balance (scheme_controls.closing_balance)
- Imp_Val_Post (for import validation)
- Periodicity (SIP frequency)
- Auto_Amount (SIP amount)
- Swap_Option (plan_auto_trxn)
- Instalment_No (SIP instalment number)
- Chan_Exg_Reg_Date (channel/exchange registration date)
- Accredit_Inv_Flag (accredited investor flag)
- NAV (current scheme NAV)

Derived from Master:
- AMC_Code
- Transaction_Sign (from transaction_types)
- Transaction_DB_CR (trxn_db_cr)
- Folio_Exists (boolean)


SECTION B: VARIABLE ASSIGNMENT (RAW DATA RETRIEVAL ONLY - NO IF/ELSE)


Following variables are retrieved via raw SQL queries or direct assignments.
NO conditional logic appears here. All IF/ELSE/CASE statements are moved to
Business Logic Section.


B.1: Sub-Transaction Types and Apply Limits


- Apply_Limits_From_Master:
  SELECT apply_limits
  FROM sub_trxn_types_master
  WHERE sub_trxn_type = Input.Sub_Transaction_Type;

- IS_SYSTEMATIC_PLAN:
  SELECT nvl(systematic, 'N')
  FROM sub_trxn_types_master
  WHERE sub_trxn_type = nvl(Input.Sub_Transaction_Type, 'N');

- IS_SYSTEMATIC_PLAN_Temp:
  SELECT nvl(systematic, 'N')
  FROM sub_trxn_types_master
  WHERE sub_trxn_type = nvl(Input.Sub_Transaction_Type, 'N');


B.2: User Master Queries


- User_Type:
  SELECT nvl(user_type, 'XYZ')
  FROM user_master
  WHERE user_id = Input.User_Code;

- DP_ID_REQUIRED:
  SELECT nvl(dp_id_required, 'N')
  FROM user_master
  WHERE user_id = Input.User_Code;


